{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 8bcdfa34d59aa8184c9c86325f0dd74b4ad2e926, tree cc80fa79c8c8af627d501046cde0deb4e7bbfdd2, on builder/r-on-main-source-20261114, all 24 artifacts, for request f2feeaca under my promise 5b532882. This verdict names all three implementations: R (request 5b5b6896, promise f68dd9c4, report 937d2721, the R note, primary), LP-1 (request fe834d8e, promise d9b356ed, report 6579e47c, the Lending descriptor) and BP-1 (request dce57e0d, promise aedda13b, report b9e98d11, the BP-1 note). `gs review --prepare` resolved all three bindings and reports at this head, with each request closing on the sealed receipt. I read the head from the shared object store. The branch is not on origin.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `packages/platform/src/application-install-reader.ts`. `applicationInstallation` already admitted Base Rules 15 at main d1585bda. The one change makes it report `platform:membership@14` for a Base install instead of falling through to the old trusted cohort's `platform:membership@7`. `platform:rules@15` belongs to `BASE_COHORT` alone, so no other family's install can take the new branch. Every other check is unchanged: an active Rules scope, the directory ref, an active `installation` item, the membership scope equal to the room's, and four digest values.\n- `packages/platform/src/application-projection-reader.ts`. The admission list gains `BC.rules`, and the comment now says \"v2 install\". After admission, the reader still requires `applicationInstallation`, the semantic and release proofs read from the immutable value store, IDs equal to the install's, the proof entry equal to the install's definition, the proof publisher equal to the item's `publisher`, and a declared projection name. It returns declaration metadata only. It grants no authority and reads no item data.\n- The callers of both readers. `projection-source.ts` reads the room's bytes and refuses any key set other than `directory,rules` or `directory,membershipDefinition,rules` with an admitted membership version. The session check sits in front of `applicationProjection` and does not change. The browser uses `membershipDefinition` to choose the invitation field shape and to require that a join receipt names that definition. A wrong value refuses a join. It cannot admit one.\n- `examples/lending/definition.ts` and the generated definition. `reserve` opens a `reservation` under the `member` grant. Its one guard refuses with `tool-day-taken` when a `held` reservation has the same `tool` and `day`. The `lapse` timed rule moves a `held` reservation to `lapsed` at its `until` and changes nothing else. `tool` and `day` are fixed slots, so a held reservation cannot move to another slot.\n- LP-1. `dap.application.json` declares `publication-paths@1` with the one prefix `shelf/`. `package.ts` spreads `manifest(...)` and replaces only `capabilities` with the same declaration, because the typed manifest has no capability option. The descriptor bytes and the package test's equality check agree.\n- The browser. `model.ts` excludes `reserve` from the circulation acts, and `annotations.ts` adds its refusal and proposal words. No screen offers reserve yet.\n- The tests. The Native projection owner now runs three rows: Counter on the declared cohort, and Counter and Lending on Base. Both Base rows check membership 14 in real metadata. Only the Lending Base row runs the negative controls: Vic's session request answers `unauthorized`, and the same projection without a session answers `forbidden`.\n- Both notes. The R note keeps gate 1 (END 5bad3c96) and the isolated follow-up (END aa2c014f) as FAIL, and states no refusal reason that the log did not show. The BP-1 note keeps the named RED e7bdf319 (`query-not-ready` at 80:59, before any reader change) apart from GREEN 0c825126 and the full gate.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main d1585bda is an ancestor. The 24 artifacts name the head, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only d1585bda 8bcdfa34`. From be552e76 to the head only the two notes change.\n- Gate. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-15-r-lp1-bp1-full-gate-attempt1/gate.log` has SHA-256 9eb67d9b…, and `result.json` has 6ce12b92…, as the request states. The log names head be552e76 and tree 4ed5786b with 0 changed files. Plain passed 4857 with 1 skipped, and Native passed 1136 with 2 skipped. Scope-scale was `omitted-by-gate`, so no Scale case ran and no Scale wall exists. The request gives the Native wall as 504081.419167 ms. Its last gate line is \"gate passed\". The gate ran on 15 November, END 1959b58d.\n- Browser filters. No changed path matches the Page or Card workflow filters. E1's Linux Page result stays dated to E1.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 25 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests, compilers or builds.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Base was the one family whose installs the projection reader refused, and its install metadata named the wrong membership. Each reader gains one branch keyed on a pin that only Base uses. The reservation uses existing forms only: an `open` act, a `none` guard on two fixed slots, and a timed rule on an explicit deadline. The LP-1 descriptor declares the one prefix that every Lending send uses.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. Both BP-1 readers keep every proof, publisher and standing check, and the session check in front of the projection does not change. The Lending Base row shows that a non-member gets no session and that a reader without a session gets `forbidden`. Membership 14 in the metadata can only make a Base join match its own receipt. Two facts for the planner:\n\n- Any member can hold every reservation. `max: 8` caps live reservations, and only `lapse` ends one. A member who opens eight reservations with a far `until` blocks every other reservation until those times pass. No staff act cancels a reservation. Ruling 02d4942a sets the day and `until` rules but says nothing on capacity. A follow-up can add a staff cancel act or bound `until`. Neither belongs in this head.\n- The Counter Base row has no negative control. The Lending Base row covers the same reader and session path.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The `package.ts` spread duplicates the descriptor's capability by hand. A `capabilities` option on `manifest` would remove the copy, and the package test catches any drift until then.\n\nQualifications that stand: gate 1 and its isolated follow-up stay FAIL. The pre-START placeholder refusal ran no command and is not a typecheck failure. The Native run uses a stand-in Git host and clock. No browser, hosted install, physical room or provider result follows. This approval authorizes no push, landing, signing or deployment. Lending 0.3.0 signing waits on the planner under ruling 841b7903. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:937d2721024251d4f8206773ceec29bfa1e6f49f","binding":"assigned","head":"8bcdfa34d59aa8184c9c86325f0dd74b4ad2e926","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5b53288257742c59d137116ab857b01949bff880\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f68dd9c48d6d54874c20a7f168b59be1c1a45efb\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d9b356ed2d2501bf34dda9287cab4d1dcfe6f36a\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:aedda13b6d272754dac9d51a11c87667db867dc5\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5b53288257742c59d137116ab857b01949bff880","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:027b2124b248a0574b9779cc46f9062351f737b3, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0d742084e6941e70937225c136a534838726af27, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:116b06f61ea216889fcfd42fdcfad8e5a48ba9